# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:68
msgid "Configuring your Development Environment"
msgstr "Mengonfigurasi Lingkungan Pengembangan Anda"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:69
msgid ""
"In order to actually compile or run SmartEdit, we need to install some "
"dependencies on your system. The easiest way to accomplish this is with our "
"`Daily PPA <https://www.smartedit.org/ppa/>`_. A PPA is an unofficial Ubuntu "
"repository, which has our software packages available to download and "
"install."
msgstr ""
"Untuk benar-benar mengompilasi atau menjalankan SmartEdit, kita perlu "
"menginstal beberapa dependensi di sistem Anda. Cara termudah untuk "
"melakukannya adalah dengan `Daily PPA <https://www.smartedit.org/ppa/>`_ "
"kami. PPA adalah repositori Ubuntu tidak resmi, yang menyediakan paket "
"perangkat lunak kami untuk diunduh dan diinstal."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:109
msgid ""
"At this point, you should have all 3 SmartEdit components source code cloned "
"into local folders, the SmartEdit daily PPA installed, and all of the "
"required development and runtime dependencies installed. This is a great "
"start, and we are now ready to start compiling some code!"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini, Anda seharusnya sudah mengkloning kode sumber ketiga "
"komponen SmartEdit ke folder lokal, menginstal PPA harian SmartEdit, dan "
"menginstal semua dependensi pengembangan dan runtime yang diperlukan. Ini "
"adalah awal yang bagus, dan sekarang kita siap mulai mengompilasi kode!"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:114
msgid "libsmartedit-audio (Build Instructions)"
msgstr "libsmartedit-audio (Instruksi Build)"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:115
msgid ""
"This library is required for audio playback and audio effects. It is based "
"on the JUCE audio framework. Here are the commands to build it:"
msgstr ""
"Perpustakaan ini diperlukan untuk pemutaran audio dan efek audio. Ini "
"berbasis pada kerangka kerja audio JUCE. Berikut adalah perintah untuk "
"membangunnya:"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:128
msgid ""
"Essentially, we are switching to the ``libsmartedit-audio/build`` folder, "
"then running ``cmake ..`` on the parent folder. This finds dependencies and "
"creates all the needed Makefiles used to compile this library. Then ``make`` "
"uses those Makefiles to compile this library, and ``make install`` installs "
"them in the location we specified. If ``CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`` isn't set, "
"the files will install to ``/usr/local/`` (by default) and ``make install`` "
"will require administrative privileges to run."
msgstr ""
"Pada dasarnya, kita beralih ke folder ``libsmartedit-audio/build``, lalu "
"menjalankan ``cmake ..`` pada folder induk. Ini mencari dependensi dan "
"membuat semua Makefile yang diperlukan untuk mengompilasi perpustakaan ini. "
"Kemudian ``make`` menggunakan Makefile tersebut untuk mengompilasi "
"perpustakaan ini, dan ``make install`` menginstalnya di lokasi yang kita "
"tentukan. Jika ``CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`` tidak disetel, file akan diinstal ke "
"``/usr/local/`` (secara default) dan ``make install`` memerlukan hak "
"administratif untuk dijalankan."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:136
msgid "libsmartedit (Build Instructions)"
msgstr "libsmartedit (Instruksi Build)"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:137
msgid ""
"This library is required for video decoding, encoding, animation, and just "
"about everything else. It does all the heavy lifting of video editing and "
"video playback. Here are the commands to build it:"
msgstr ""
"Perpustakaan ini diperlukan untuk decoding video, encoding, animasi, dan "
"hampir semua hal lainnya. Ini melakukan semua pekerjaan berat pengeditan "
"video dan pemutaran video. Berikut adalah perintah untuk membangunnya:"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:149
msgid ""
"Essentially, we are switching to the ``libsmartedit/build`` folder, then "
"running ``cmake ..`` on the parent folder. This finds dependencies and "
"creates all the needed Makefiles used to compile this library. Then ``make`` "
"uses those Makefiles to compile this library. Because we provided the "
"location of our compiled ``libsmartedit-audio`` installation, that version of "
"the library will be used instead of the system version (if any)."
msgstr ""
"Pada dasarnya, kita beralih ke folder ``libsmartedit/build``, lalu "
"menjalankan ``cmake ..`` pada folder induk. Ini mencari dependensi dan "
"membuat semua Makefile yang diperlukan untuk mengompilasi perpustakaan ini. "
"Kemudian ``make`` menggunakan Makefile tersebut untuk mengompilasi "
"perpustakaan ini. Karena kita menyediakan lokasi instalasi ``libsmartedit-"
"audio`` yang sudah dikompilasi, versi perpustakaan tersebut akan digunakan "
"menggantikan versi sistem (jika ada)."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:156
msgid ""
"We don't install our ``libsmartedit`` after building, because we don't need "
"to. For testing purposes, we can tell SmartEdit to use ``libsmartedit`` right "
"from our ``build`` directory."
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak menginstal ``libsmartedit`` setelah membangunnya, karena tidak "
"perlu. Untuk tujuan pengujian, kita dapat memberitahu SmartEdit untuk "
"menggunakan ``libsmartedit`` langsung dari direktori ``build`` kami."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:160
msgid "Language Bindings"
msgstr "Binding Bahasa"

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../developers.rst:161
msgid ""
"The ``libsmartedit`` API is available in several languages through SWIG "
"bindings.  Python is used by the SmartEdit user interface, and we also "
"provide Ruby and Java bindings.  Experimental support for Godot **4.4** is "
"included for developers who wish to integrate video editing features into "
"the Godot game engine.  All of these bindings map to the same C++ codebase "
"so you can edit video from the environment you prefer."
msgstr ""
"API ``libsmartedit`` tersedia dalam beberapa bahasa melalui binding SWIG. "
"Python digunakan oleh antarmuka pengguna SmartEdit, dan kami juga menyediakan "
"binding Ruby dan Java. Dukungan eksperimental untuk Godot **4.4** disertakan "
"bagi pengembang yang ingin mengintegrasikan fitur pengeditan video ke dalam "
"mesin game Godot. Semua binding ini memetakan ke basis kode C++ yang sama "
"sehingga Anda dapat mengedit video dari lingkungan yang Anda pilih."

